    "🏛️ <strong>KISS Principle:</strong> The most resilient architecture is the one that solves the problem with the minimum number of moving parts.",
    "🏛️ <strong>YAGNI Principle:</strong> Resist adding speculative abstractions or configuration layers for hypothetical requirements you do not yet have.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Single Responsibility (SRP):</strong> Every module, class, or package should have one—and only one—reason to change.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Open/Closed Principle (OCP):</strong> Software entities should be open for extension through interfaces, but closed for invasive modification.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Liskov Substitution (LSP):</strong> Subtypes must be substitutable for their base types without altering program correctness or expectations.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Interface Segregation (ISP):</strong> Many client-specific fine-grained interfaces are far superior to a single bloated, all-encompassing interface.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Dependency Inversion (DIP):</strong> High-level domain logic should depend on clean abstractions rather than concrete low-level implementations.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Composition over Inheritance:</strong> Favor composing small structs with distinct capabilities over deep, fragile class inheritance trees.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Fail Fast Principle:</strong> Validate function arguments and invariants upfront; return early or error out immediately before performing work.",
    "🏛️ <strong>DDD Ubiquitous Language:</strong> Adopt identical domain terminology across source code, database tables, and team design discussions.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Hexagonal Architecture:</strong> Decouple core domain business logic from external frameworks, databases, and UI layers via ports and adapters.",
    "🏛️ <strong>CQRS Pattern:</strong> Separate read query models from write command mutators to independently optimize scale, caching, and schemas.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Event-Driven Architecture:</strong> Decouple services by publishing asynchronous domain events upon state changes rather than tight synchronous RPCs.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Strangler Fig Pattern:</strong> Incrementally migrate legacy monoliths by routing endpoints to new microservices behind a facade proxy until replaced.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Boy Scout Rule:</strong> Always check in code cleaner than you found it, making small continuous improvements on every commit.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Separation of Concerns:</strong> Divide application responsibilities into clean layers: Presentation, Application, Domain, and Infrastructure.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Immutability by Default:</strong> Immutable data structures cannot mutate after creation, completely eliminating race conditions across threads.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Clean Architecture:</strong> Source code dependencies must strictly point inward toward core domain business entities and use cases.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Repository Pattern:</strong> Abstract data persistence operations behind repository interfaces to enable straightforward unit testing with in-memory mocks.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Factory Pattern:</strong> Centralize instantiation logic of complex polymorphic objects to decouple callers from concrete constructors.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Strategy Pattern:</strong> Define interchangeable algorithms encapsulated behind a common interface, selectable dynamically at runtime.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Observer Pattern:</strong> Broadcast state transitions to decoupled subscriber listeners without tight coupling between publisher and consumers.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Decorator Pattern:</strong> Dynamically attach new behaviors (e.g. logging, metrics, caching) to objects by wrapping them in matching interfaces.",
    "🏛️ <strong>DRY vs Premature Abstraction:</strong> A little duplication is far cheaper than the wrong abstraction; wait for clear repeated patterns before factoring out.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Pure Functions:</strong> Pure functions have no hidden side effects and return identical outputs for given inputs, making them effortlessly testable.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Tell, Don't Ask:</strong> Instruct objects to execute behaviors internally rather than querying their private state to make decisions externally.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Law of Demeter:</strong> A module should talk only to its immediate collaborators, avoiding long method call chains like <code>a.getB().getC().doD()</code>.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Null Object Pattern:</strong> Return a neutral object with no-op behaviors instead of raw <code>null</code> to eradicate repetitive null-check boilerplate.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Command-Query Separation:</strong> A method should either perform a state-modifying action or return data, but never combine both in one call.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Value Objects:</strong> Model domain concepts (e.g. Money, Email, GeoCoordinates) as immutable value objects identified by their values rather than IDs.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Bounded Contexts:</strong> Split large enterprise systems into isolated Bounded Contexts with explicit model boundaries and domain definitions.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Anti-Corruption Layer (ACL):</strong> Build a translation adapter between new services and legacy systems to prevent legacy models polluting clean domains.",
    "🏛️ <strong>Semantic Naming:</strong> Name methods clearly by what they accomplish for the caller; avoid vague names like <code>process()</code>, <code>manager()</code>, or <code>data()</code>.",
